## W4D3: GPUs in the scheduler's ledger Predict Questions

- Your node has some number of CPUs (kubectl describe node, Capacity). If a pod requests 64 CPUs, what exactly happens: an error on apply, a pod that crashes, or something else?
  >  something else, kubectl apply and the pod won't crash. It will be accepteed by K8s but it'll be pending since the scheduler can't find a node with available CPU.

- Your pod has one card. A teammate's pod already holds it, and you request nvidia.com/gpu: 1. Same question. Will the error message name the GPU?
  >  the pod is accepted but stays Pending because there is no available GPU.

- A neighbour pod burns all the CPU it can get with no limit. Your serving pod's /health latency: unchanged, somewhat worse, or catastrophically worse? Now the neighbour gets limits: cpu: 500m. What changes?
  > the unlimited cpu neighbour  makes the /health latency worse, but with a 500m limit the neighbour  will be throttled reaching the limit and the serving latency ican be more predictable  
